# Scenario 'time_warnings': the connection-time notice ("つうしんじかんが まもなく 10ぷんに なります"). Timer A counts the seconds of a connection; the
# session loops compare it with the minute of the next notice ([C26E], first 9:30) and open the notice dialog (50:4000 family) once it is reached.
# Round 1 never stayed connected that long. Each segment starts with a power cycle (`reset`) from the state of 'mail_inbox' and keeps one session
# open for more than ten minutes of emulated time: (1) メールサーバ "かくにんしてから": idle on the first mail's icon bar; (2) じどうでぜんぶけす
# with a slow fake POP3 server (`net latency=3000`: every server answer is readable 3000 frames = 50 s after the request); (3) the same through
# the hidden variant (SELECT+LEFT), second button; (4) おくる/うけとる with latency 3000, the notice answered with A (はい); (5) おくる/うけとる with
# latency 1800, the notice answered RIGHT+A (いいえ), which hangs up. A is pressed every 1500 frames from minute 8 on to answer whichever dialog is
# up. Screen names = my reading of the screenshots. Starts from the state left by 'mail_inbox' (five mails on the fake POP3 server).
net latency=2
# ---- check idle (notice while waiting on the icon bar)
reset
wait 400
waitstable 60 max 600
gap 30
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
tap DOWN x5
wait 30
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
net latency=2
tap A
waitstable 60 max 900
wait 30000
tap A
wait 1500
tap A
wait 1500
tap A
wait 1500
tap A
wait 1500
tap A
wait 1500
tap A
wait 1500
tap A
wait 1500
tap A
wait 1500
tap A
wait 1500
tap A
wait 1500
shot end
net latency=2
